-- WITHAL is standalone: nothing may follow it, because WITH already covers an
-- override and one construction should not have two spellings
-- (TYPICALLY-ONE-BEHAVIOUR-SPEC.md T1, ruled by Meng 2026-10-09).
-- This file is a parse error. The override is written WITH:
-- `Paint WITH label IS "gloss"`.

DECLARE Paint
  HAS label IS A STRING TYPICALLY "plain"
      coats IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 2

GIVETH A Paint
glossy MEANS Paint WITHAL label IS "gloss"
